    <briefdescription>
<para>Argument and input validation errors. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classcslt_1_1ArgumentError" kindref="compound">ArgumentError</ref> represents errors related to invalid function arguments, null pointers, out-of-bounds access, and other input validation failures.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Example Usage:</title><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>Using<sp/>default<sp/>message</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">throw<sp/>ArgumentError();<sp/><sp/>//<sp/>&quot;Invalid<sp/>argument&quot;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>Using<sp/>custom<sp/>message</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">throw<sp/>ArgumentError(&quot;Index<sp/>5<sp/>is<sp/>out<sp/>of<sp/>bounds<sp/>for<sp/>array<sp/>of<sp/>size<sp/>3&quot;);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
